{
  "repository": "sv5byp/FTFlow",
  "tag": "r172",
  "title": "FTflow r172 - Complete signed automatic upgrade with RTTY and CW Bot",
  "body": "FTflow r172 continues the complete FTFlow line, including the existing weak-signal modes, RTTY Bot and CW Bot.\n\nAUTOMATIC UPGRADE\nOlder FTFlow releases that already support signed automatic updates can upgrade through Help > Check for updates. Accept the update and let the program restart. The signed update includes the clock helper, CW model and automation runtime; no separate ZIP extraction or file copying is required. Settings, activation records, contacts and logs are retained. Subsequent update checks are available in this version too.\n\nThe program waits for transmission/automatic QSO to stop before installing. Companion files are verified and staged before installation; existing managed files are backed up under update-backups. An interrupted companion transaction is recovered before radio initialization. If a file is locked or the folder cannot be written, close other FTFlow tools and restart to retry. Keep update-backups for recovery assistance. Program-file backups from the legacy updater are also retained. Settings and logs are excluded from both transactions.\n\nFULL PORTABLE DOWNLOAD\nFor a fresh installation, or for r171 (which has no updater menu), extract the complete portable ZIP into a new folder and run FTFlow.exe. Keep all included files together. Older releases without the signed updater also require the full download once.\n\nCLOCK\nAutomatic clock synchronization defaults OFF in a new profile. The user's saved ON/OFF choice is preserved. First activation of the updated helper may request Windows permission once. Optional clock synchronization requires Windows 10/11 and Windows PowerShell 5.1. No clock task is installed or run merely by extracting this package with synchronization OFF.\n\nExisting decoder/DSP/AFC, F1-F12, multichannel CW, 90-day access levels and radio/audio/CAT backends are unchanged. Based on MSHV by LZ2HV, GNU GPL; DeepCW model by VE3NEA, MIT. Original licenses and attribution are included. No proprietary CW Skimmer code is included.\n\nValidation uses isolated profiles, simulated radio routes, file-lock/crash recovery and signed legacy-updater transactions. No physical radio/CAT/PTT/audio operation or actual clock correction/task installation was exercised. Actual operator acceptance remains necessary.\n\n366 automated software assertions passed, plus a native legacy-updater arm/commit/restart migration verifying all 71 companions, and final portable startup/icon checks.\n\n",
